On 16 May 2003 at 3:40, sshiskom wrote:

> On the other hand, what is {bu'u ibu}? Isn't {ibu} a letteral
> for "i"?

Yes. But lerfu can also be used as pro-sumti; if they are not 
explicitly assigned with {goi}, they are, by convention, taken to refer 
to "the most recent sumti whose name or description begins in Lojban 
with that lerfu". See 
http://www.lojban.org/publications/reference_grammar/chapter17.html#s9

Hence, {.ibu} could reasonably refer to {la .Inisfris}.

